---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site, APPS } from '../../content';
const path = '/compare';
const title = 'Shopify SMS marketing app comparisons';
const desc = 'Browse published Shopify messaging comparisons by workflow, channel ownership and migration needs, including historical review contexts.';
// Authored source-page inventory: retain both orientations when both pages exist.
const authoredRoutes = [
  "activecampaign-vs-klaviyo",
  "aftership-email-vs-klaviyo",
  "attentive-vs-activecampaign",
  "attentive-vs-mailchimp",
  "brevo-vs-mailchimp",
  "brevo-vs-omnisend",
  "drip-vs-activecampaign",
  "drip-vs-attentive",
  "drip-vs-brevo",
  "drip-vs-mailchimp",
  "drip-vs-postscript",
  "drip-vs-sendlane",
  "firepush-vs-omnisend",
  "klaviyo-vs-drip",
  "klaviyo-vs-mailchimp",
  "klaviyo-vs-omnisend",
  "klaviyo-vs-postscript",
  "klaviyo-vs-privy",
  "klaviyo-vs-shopify-email",
  "klaviyo-vs-yotpo-email-sms",
  "marsello-vs-klaviyo",
  "marsello-vs-yotpo-email-sms",
  "omnisend-vs-attentive",
  "omnisend-vs-drip",
  "omnisend-vs-mailchimp",
  "omnisend-vs-postscript",
  "omnisend-vs-privy",
  "omnisend-vs-shopify-email",
  "omnisend-vs-yotpo-email-sms",
  "postscript-vs-activecampaign",
  "postscript-vs-aftership-email",
  "postscript-vs-attentive",
  "postscript-vs-brevo",
  "postscript-vs-mailchimp",
  "postscript-vs-sendlane",
  "postscript-vs-smsbump",
  "privy-vs-activecampaign",
  "privy-vs-attentive",
  "privy-vs-brevo",
  "privy-vs-drip",
  "privy-vs-justuno",
  "privy-vs-mailchimp",
  "privy-vs-postscript",
  "recart-vs-postscript",
  "rejoiner-vs-klaviyo",
  "rejoiner-vs-sendlane",
  "sendlane-vs-klaviyo",
  "sequenzy-vs-drip",
  "sequenzy-vs-klaviyo",
  "sequenzy-vs-mailchimp",
  "sequenzy-vs-omnisend",
  "sequenzy-vs-privy",
  "sequenzy-vs-shopify-email",
  "sequenzy-vs-yotpo-email-sms",
  "tinyemail-vs-mailchimp",
  "tinyemail-vs-shopify-email",
  "yotpo-email-sms-vs-activecampaign",
  "yotpo-email-sms-vs-attentive",
  "yotpo-email-sms-vs-drip",
  "yotpo-email-sms-vs-klaviyo",
  "yotpo-email-sms-vs-mailchimp",
  "yotpo-email-sms-vs-omnisend",
  "yotpo-email-sms-vs-postscript",
  "yotpo-email-sms-vs-privy"
];
const names = new Map(APPS.map((app) => [app.slug, app.name]));
const comparisons = authoredRoutes.map((slug) => ({
  slug,
  label: slug.split('-vs-').map((part) => names.get(part) ?? part).join(' vs '),
  historical: /yotpo-email-sms|smsbump|firepush/.test(slug),
}));
const groups = [
  { title: 'Current workflow evaluation', pages: comparisons.filter((p) => !p.historical) },
  { title: 'Historical review and migration contexts', pages: comparisons.filter((p) => p.historical) },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-14 md:py-20">
    <header class="max-w-4xl">
      <p class="badge">Comparison hub</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Shopify messaging comparisons by job</h1>
      <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Start with the workflow you need to operate: a product drop, cart recovery, customer education or a sender migration. These links open published editorial comparisons, not a promise that every product supports every channel or that every catalog pairing has a guide.</p>
    </header>
    <article class="prose-shopify card mt-10">
      <h2>Choose a route for your decision</h2>
      <p>If you are comparing a dedicated SMS workflow with a shared email and SMS operation, start with <a href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-postscript">Klaviyo vs Postscript</a> and document who owns replies, campaign approval and purchase exits. If your decision centers on lifecycle email and an event bridge, use <a href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-klaviyo">Sequenzy vs Klaviyo</a> to frame the integration questions; demonstrate the required Shopify events and channel access in your own account before choosing.</p>
      <p>For a catalog launch, rehearse waitlist priority, inventory changes and cancellation of queued reminders after purchase. For an education or replenishment journey, verify identity matching, event freshness and permission for each channel. Use the <a href="/for">store guides</a> for merchandising context and <a href="/use-cases">workflow guides</a> for the message job.</p>
      <h3>Current evaluation versus historical jobs</h3>
      <p>The historical group is for reading older comparisons and planning exports, suppression preservation and replacement workflows. A Yotpo Email &amp; SMS, SMSBump or Firepush link is not evidence of current messaging availability or an invitation to purchase a legacy service. Confirm current product access and support directly with the provider before using any review as a buying decision. The current workflow group also requires account-specific confirmation of channels, destinations and plan access.</p>
    </article>
    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2">
      {groups.map((group) => (
        <section>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-black">{group.title}</h2>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2">
            {group.pages.map((p) => (
              <li><a class="link text-lg" href={`/compare/${p.slug}`}>{p.label}</a></li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </section>
      ))}
    </div>
    <article class="prose-shopify card mt-12">
      <h2>Make the shortlist operational</h2>
      <p>Capture the opt-in source, disclosure and channel status you need to retain. Rehearse an opt-out, a duplicate profile, a delayed order event and a purchase while a message is queued. Assign an owner to exceptions, replies and cross-channel collision rules. Check the applicable sending restrictions for your audience with qualified advice; a successful test is not legal clearance. See <a href="/guides/consent">consent</a> and <a href="/guides/tcpa">sending-rule considerations</a>.</p>
      <p>Request a quote for your destinations, contact count, message mix, peak demand and required integrations. Compare net sales after discounts and returns, less product, fulfillment, platform, messaging and incremental support costs; do not subtract discounts or returns again. If measuring lift, compare contribution per eligible customer across comparable treatment and holdout groups over the same window. Choose the window around the purchase cycle and sufficient observations, rather than a fixed pilot length. Use <a href="/guides/pricing">pricing economics</a> to prepare the questions.</p>
      <p>For limited-stock drops, make scarcity messages depend on live inventory and stop them when the offer expires. For gifting, separate purchaser and recipient identities before scheduling follow-up. For repeat purchases, test replenishment timing against the customer's actual order history. Keep an operator-owned calendar and review <a href="/guides/campaign-restraint">campaign restraint</a> when messages overlap. Browse the <a href="/apps">app directory</a> for individual reviews after identifying the job you need to prove.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
